rld/europe/polish-swimmer-becomes-the-first-person-to-swim-from-sweden-to-poland-across-the-baltic-sea-in-55-hours/articleshow/132902885.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/polish-swimmer-becomes-the-first-person-to-swim-from-sweden-to-poland-across-the-baltic-sea-in-55-hours/articleshow/132902885.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T13:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132902961,imgsize-1002557.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists placed 42 sea sponges in a polluted Spanish port]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132896260.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-placed-42-sea-sponges-in-a-polluted-spanish-port-455-days-later-one-species-had-thrived-while-four-others-died/articleshow/132896260.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-placed-42-sea-sponges-in-a-polluted-spanish-port-455-days-later-one-species-had-thrived-while-four-others-died/articleshow/132896260.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T13:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132896260,imgsize-80386.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Lithops werneri: Tiny Namibian plant survives by disguising itself as a pebble]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132896267.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/lithops-werneri-the-tiny-namibian-plant-that-survives-by-disguising-itself-as-a-pebble-fewer-than-200-now-remain-in-the-wild/articleshow/132896267.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/lithops-werneri-the-tiny-namibian-plant-that-survives-by-disguising-itself-as-a-pebble-fewer-than-200-now-remain-in-the-wild/articleshow/132896267.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T13:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132896267,imgsize-107142.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[After Japan's devastating 2011 tsunami, volunteers have planted more than 680,000 trees to protect the coast from future tsunamis]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132896673.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a remarkable effort to enhance its coastal protection, Japan is planting over 680,000 native trees through the Chinju no Mori Project. This initiative, which complements existing concrete seawalls established after the 2011 tsunami, employs the innovative Miyawaki Method. By drawing inspiration from ancient guardian forests, these new dense forests will not only serve as a natural barrier against disasters but also provide numerous ecological advantages.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/after-japans-devastating-2011-tsunami-volunteers-have-planted-more-than-680000-trees-to-protect-the-coast-from-future-tsunamis/articleshow/132896673.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/after-japans-devastating-2011-tsunami-volunteers-have-planted-more-than-680000-trees-to-protect-the-coast-from-future-tsunamis/articleshow/132896673.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T12:00:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132896673,imgsize-1450385.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Operation Eau de Fraud': Chicago YouTuber charged after replacing luxury perfumes with modeling clay]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132900846.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A YouTuber from Chicago has been charged in connection with an intricate perfume return fraud scheme. He allegedly swapped high-end fragrances for modeling clay and resealed packaging. During a search of his apartment, authorities confiscated hundreds of perfume bottles valued at approximately $250,000. The case was initiated after a luxury retailer flagged concerning returns of modified items, underscoring the escalating issue of return fraud in the retail sector.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/operation-eau-de-fraud-chicago-youtuber-charged-after-replacing-luxury-perfumes-with-modeling-clay-in-return-scam-police-seize-250000-worth-of-fragrances/articleshow/132900846.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/operation-eau-de-fraud-chicago-youtuber-charged-after-replacing-luxury-perfumes-with-modeling-clay-in-return-scam-police-seize-250000-worth-of-fragrances/articleshow/132900846.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T12:49:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132900846,imgsize-671385.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New Whale Stomach Bacteria Found: Scientists identify 3 Helicobacter genotypes]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132896270.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discover-three-new-stomach-bacteria-after-21-years-of-research-that-may-be-linked-to-chronic-stomach-disease-in-pygmy-sperm-whales/articleshow/132896270.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-discover-three-new-stomach-bacteria-after-21-years-of-research-that-may-be-linked-to-chronic-stomach-disease-in-pygmy-sperm-whales/articleshow/132896270.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T12:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132896270,imgsize-24898.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California’s western monarch migration hits third-lowest count at 12,260]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132898173.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[This winter's survey of the western monarch butterfly revealed over 12,000 individuals, a small rise from last year. Despite this slight increase, conservationists remain alarmed as numbers are still critically low. Ongoing challenges such as habitat loss and environmental stressors severely impact the butterfly population. Conservation initiatives are actively working on restoring habitats and engaging the community in monitoring efforts.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/californias-winter-monarch-migration-has-collapsed-from-millions-in-the-1990s-to-12260-butterflies-in-2025-the-third-lowest-count-ever-recorded/articleshow/132898173.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/californias-winter-monarch-migration-has-collapsed-from-millions-in-the-1990s-to-12260-butterflies-in-2025-the-third-lowest-count-ever-recorded/articleshow/132898173.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T12:23:32+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132898173,imgsize-258147.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[The insect that carries its own bomb: How the bombardier beetle turns chemistry into a weapon]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132895664.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Bombardier beetles possess a unique defense mechanism involving explosive chemical sprays.  These insects mix chemicals to create a hot, noxious spray for protection.  Their specialized internal structures allow them to survive these powerful self-inflicted explosions.  Bombardier beetles can fire their chemical bombs multiple times before needing to escape.  These fascinating insects have evolved remarkable adaptations for survival in various ecosystems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/the-insect-that-carries-its-own-bomb-how-the-bombardier-beetle-turns-chemistry-into-a-weapon-against-its-predators/articleshow/132895664.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/the-insect-that-carries-its-own-bomb-how-the-bombardier-beetle-turns-chemistry-into-a-weapon-against-its-predators/articleshow/132895664.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T11:47:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132895664,imgsize-96309.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists prove Charles Darwin's 150-year-old theory right with the help of an insect-eating plant]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132894636.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A breakthrough in plant science has validated Charles Darwin's historic conjecture surrounding carnivorous Saxifraga species. Researchers discovered that these plants ensnare small gnats with sticky hairs, emitting fragrances that lure their prey. Chemical tests confirmed that insects provide essential nutrients upon capture, as showcased by isotope labeling. This pivotal finding sheds light on the complex interactions and nutritional strategies of plant carnivory in mountainous regions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-identify-an-insect-eating-plant-that-just-proved-charles-darwins-150-year-old-theory-right/articleshow/132894636.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-identify-an-insect-eating-plant-that-just-proved-charles-darwins-150-year-old-theory-right/articleshow/132894636.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T11:29:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132894636,imgsize-123961.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['We'll know in 48 hours': Trump warns Iran to open Hormuz or get 'hit very hard']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132895176.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/well-know-in-48-hours-trump-warns-iran-to-open-hormuz-or-get-hit-very-hard/articleshow/132895176.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/well-know-in-48-hours-trump-warns-iran-to-open-hormuz-or-get-hit-very-hard/articleshow/132895176.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T11:35:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132895176,imgsize-93540.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Leonardo DiCaprio and Jeff Bezos unveil $200 million mission to save 100 endangered species]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132890256.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A new $200 million Phoenix Species Project will support 100 critically endangered species. This initiative is a collaboration between Re:wild and the Bezos Earth Fund. The project aims to provide significant financial backing for long-term recovery programs. It will bolster existing conservation efforts and expand habitat protection initiatives. Local organizations will receive crucial funding and technical assistance for their vital work.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/leonardo-dicaprio-and-jeff-bezos-launch-200-million-project-to-save-100-of-worlds-most-threatened-species-from-salamanders-and-pangolins-to-rare-pigs/articleshow/132890256.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/leonardo-dicaprio-and-jeff-bezos-launch-200-million-project-to-save-100-of-worlds-most-threatened-species-from-salamanders-and-pangolins-to-rare-pigs/articleshow/132890256.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-05T10:11:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132890256,imgsize-94797.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists clone rare Queen of Sheba Orchid, growing 1,000 plants in five years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132794742.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2021-australian-scientists-cloned-one-seed-of-the-queen-of-sheba-orchid-five-years-later-it-produced-1000-plants-and-its-first-flower/articleshow/132794742.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2021-australian-scientists-cloned-one-seed-of-the-queen-of-sheba-orchid-five-years-later-it-produ